  {
    "id": "caseops/tilde-empty-line-fails",
    "buffer": [
      "ab",
      ""
    ],
    "cursor": [
      1,
      1
    ],
    "keys": "xj~u",
    "groups": [
      "x",
      "j",
      "~",
      "u"
    ],
    "note": "~ on an empty line beeps, changes nothing, and creates no undo block — the u must undo the x. Grouped so the beep cannot abort the u.",
    "encodedKeys": "xj~u",
    "expect": {
      "registers": {
        "\"": {
          "type": "v",
          "text": "a"
        },
        "-": {
          "type": "v",
          "text": "a"
        }
      },
      "buffer": [
        "ab",
        ""
      ],
      "cursor": [
        1,
        1
      ],
      "error": "",
      "curswant": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "caseops/guu-blank-line-still-mints-undo",
    "buffer": [
      "ab",
      "   "
    ],
    "cursor": [
      1,
      1
    ],
    "keys": "xjguuu",
    "groups": [
      "x",
      "j",
      "guu",
      "u"
    ],
    "note": "guu over a whitespace-only line changes nothing, yet still creates an undo block — a case operator that RUNS always does, so the u burns on it and the x survives. Contrast caseops/tilde-empty-line-fails, where the command genuinely fails and mints nothing.",
